<figure class="cache-figure" data-hot-key-load>
 <p class="figure-title">More aggregate capacity, the same concentrated work</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Primaries <select aria-label="Number of primaries" data-shards><option value="3">3</option><option value="6">6</option></select></label><label>Requests for one hot key <input data-hot type="range" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="50" /><output data-percent>50%</output></label></div>
 <p class="figure-note">240 requests/s offered · illustrative budget: 100 work units/s per primary · every request costs one unit</p>
 <div class="cluster-load-legend"><span>■ Hot key</span><span>▧ Other keys</span><span>│ Per-primary budget</span></div>
 <div class="cluster-load-rows" data-rows></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>Try six primaries without changing the hot-key share. Other-key work is ideally balanced; the hot key remains indivisible and resides on A. All bars use the same 0–240 work-units/s scale. This is offered work against an assumed budget, not measured Redis throughput, queueing or dropped requests. A real workload has unequal operation and response costs.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{hotKeyLoad}from'../../lib/caching/cluster.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-hot-key-load]').forEach(root=>{const shards=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-shards]')!,hot=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-hot]')!;const render=()=>{const s=hotKeyLoad(Number(shards.value),Number(hot.value));root.querySelector('[data-percent]')!.textContent=`${hot.value}%`;hot.setAttribute('aria-valuetext',`${hot.value} per cent`);const rows=root.querySelector('[data-rows]')!;rows.replaceChildren(...s.nodes.map((node,i)=>{const row=document.createElement('div');row.className='cluster-load-row';const name=document.createElement('b');name.textContent=String.fromCharCode(65+i);const track=document.createElement('div');track.className='cluster-load-track';track.setAttribute('role','img');track.setAttribute('aria-label',`Primary ${name.textContent}: ${node.hot} hot plus ${node.cold} other, budget100`);for(const[type,value]of[['hot',node.hot],['cold',node.cold]] as const){const segment=document.createElement('i');segment.className=type;segment.style.width=`${value/s.demand*100}%`;track.append(segment);}const mark=document.createElement('b');mark.style.left=`${s.budget/s.demand*100}%`;track.append(mark);const value=document.createElement('span');value.textContent=String(Math.round(node.total*10)/10);row.append(name,track,value);return row;}));root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=s.excess>0?`Primary A receives ${s.nodes[0].total.toFixed(0)} work units/s against its budget of 100. ${s.excess.toFixed(0)} units/s exceed a primary’s budget even though aggregate capacity is ${s.nodes.length*100}. Adding shards spreads the other keys; it does not divide this key.`:'Every primary is within its assumed budget. The work fits because its distribution fits, not simply because the cluster has enough aggregate capacity.';};shards.onchange=render;hot.oninput=render;render();});
</script>
